;; Signals with handlers (AX5.4; AX5-DESIGN §1): x86i's own layer over crt (AXS52 (a)): rt_sigaction, rt_sigprocmask,
;; sigaltstack and rt_sigreturn, and the frame Linux builds for a handler on x86-64, its layout from the psABI and musl's
;; arch/x86_64/bits/signal.h (MIT; the kernel's source not read), held to the native's by the lockstep:
;;
;;	frame+0    the restorer's address (the handler's return address)
;;	frame+8    ucontext: uc_flags, uc_link, uc_stack (ss_sp, ss_flags, ss_size)
;;	frame+48   mcontext: gregs[23] (R8-R15, RDI, RSI, RBP, RBX, RDX, RAX, RCX, RSP, RIP, EFL, CSGSFS, ERR, TRAPNO, OLDMASK, CR2),
;;	           the fpstate's address (frame+232), eight reserved words
;;	frame+304  uc_sigmask (the kernel's eight bytes)
;;	frame+312  siginfo (128 bytes)
;;
;; the fpstate (an XSAVE image: the FXSAVE area, its software-reserved words naming the extended area, the XSAVE header)
;; above it, 64-aligned, below the red zone's 128 bytes (or the alternate stack's top); the frame 16-aligned less 8, as at a
;; function's entry. RDI the signal, RSI the siginfo, RDX the ucontext, RAX 0; DF and TF cleared.


